# Embedded dashboard build output: vite builds the React bundle into crates/httpapi/web-dist/
# (see crates/httpapi/src/web.rs). Like Go's uncommitted web/dist, the bundle is NOT committed —
# only the .gitkeep anchor is, so rust-embed's #[folder = "web-dist/"] compiles on a clean checkout.
/crates/httpapi/web-dist/*
!/crates/httpapi/web-dist/.gitkeep
# The claude backend writes this MCP server manifest into the run's working directory so the
# dispatched agent can reach `rhapsodyd mcp`. It holds absolute, machine-local paths and is
# regenerated per run, so it is never committed — a dispatched run working IN this repo would
# otherwise sweep it up.
/.symphony-mcp.json
